text:
claire: Heads up — got a few reports from QA about the console on narrow phones. Two issues: 1) table column headers overlap the action bar when sticky; 2) sidebar open pushes content and causes horizontal scrollbar to jump. i pasted screenshots.

diego: thanks. what breakpoints were you testing? i noticed issues under 380px on Android emulators.

claire: mainly 375px (iPhone SE) and 360px. The overlap seems to appear when `position: sticky` header hits top and we also render a compact action bar with chips.

riley: idea: switch to a compact header variant when width < 420px that reduces padding and hides non-essential columns. we could prioritize columns: name, status, age. rest go to a row details panel.

aria-bot: automated accessibility check: 1) sticky header loses focus order in compact variant (ARIA-11); 2) action icons have < 44px touch targets (WCAG-touchsize-2).

noah: FWIW the sidebar problem is because we animate width and not transform, so layout recalculates. try moving to transform for visible animation and keep `overflow-x: hidden` on the page wrapper. example snippet: 
```css
.page-wrap { overflow-x: hidden; }
.side-drawer { position: fixed; transform: translateX(-100%); transition: transform 220ms ease; }
.side-drawer.open { transform: translateX(0); }
```

claire: good call @noah. but can't make it fixed for all pages; some dashboards rely on in-flow placement for anchor positioning of tooltips. maybe conditional fixed for narrow widths only.

riley: for column-priority collapsing i suggest a CSS-first approach: use `display: contents` for table rows and collapse cells into a stacked flow via pseudo-headers when width < 420px. this keeps semantics for screen readers. quick example: 
```css
@media (max-width:420px) {
  table tr td { display: block; }
  table tr td::before { content: attr(data-label); font-weight:600; }
}
```

diego: careful: `display: contents` loses focusable semantics in some browsers. test on iOS Safari. also performance with large tables could suffer. maybe only enable stacked view for rows < 1000 or when pagination < 50.

aria-bot: note: when cells are block-level the visual reading order differs from DOM order; ensure `aria-labelledby` or `data-label` matches accessible names. rule id: WCAG-name-1.

noah: microcopy nit — the compact filter chip text `Active` vs `Only active` confuses users. prefer `Show active` as the action label.

claire: agreed, we'll change to `Show active`. also riley can you prototype the stacked rows + preserved header on top for small screens? try to preserve virtualization by rendering visible windows only.

riley: yep i'll mock it. plan: 1) header variant at <=420px, 2) stacked rows with data-labels, 3) sidebar animation via transform on small widths only. i'll put a WIP PR for design review tomorrow.

claire: timeline sounds good. action items: @noah add `overflow-x:hidden` wrapper conditional at <=420px; @diego smoke test iOS Safari; @riley prototype stacked rows + virtualized render; @aria-bot re-run checks after PR. thanks :raised_hands:
